Subject: [PATCH] abl-symbols: accept node labels restored by newer dtc

dtc 1.8.1 decompiles a DTB with -@ into labeled nodes when __symbols__ is
present. After adding the symbol union, the sink has 1781 labels. The
existing parser incorrectly reports that this node is absent. Accept labels
before the node name without relaxing the node-name or brace checks.
Applied only to a scratch copy; the pinned upstream clone stays read-only.

--- a/tools/lib/abl-symbols.py
+++ b/tools/lib/abl-symbols.py
@@ -35,7 +35,11 @@
 
 def extract_block(text, node_name):
     """Return the body of a top-level node, or None when it is absent."""
-    marker = re.search(rf"^\s*{re.escape(node_name)}\s*\{{\s*$", text, re.MULTILINE)
+    marker = re.search(
+        rf"^\s*(?:[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*:\s*)*"
+        rf"{re.escape(node_name)}\s*\{{\s*$",
+        text, re.MULTILINE,
+    )
     if marker is None:
         return None
     start = marker.end()
